/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  compare_visc_liquid_ammonia
  ===========================

  Liquid-viscosity Andrade correlation for pure ammonia (NH3), 235-300 K.
  This case is SEALED: it runs its own copy, constant/components/NH3.dat,
  whose Andrade pair was fitted to the Engineering Toolbox table -- a no-grant
  source (CLAUDE.md 10) -- and, measured against the reference correlation
  (Monogenidou, Assael & Huber, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 47, 023102 (2018),
  Table 6), is +10 % at 240 K and +65 % at 300 K.  Since 2026-10-11 (DEV.md
  4c C65 item c) the CATALOGUE record data/standards/components/NH3.dat
  carries a fit to that Table 6 (AAD 0.51 % over 200-320 K; 0.253 mPa.s at
  the normal boiling point, against Table 6's 0.2510 at 240 K).  This copy
  keeps the old pair until the case is re-imported, and check_source_licence
  pins it until then; the golden pins only the scan's point counts, so the
  re-import moves no golden row.  Note this case scans a SINGLE method (Andrade) -- it is a
  single-correlation curve, not a multi-method comparison.  Ammonia is liquid
  only under pressure in this T window; viscosity_liquid is a pure-T
  correlation, so the state P is immaterial to the value.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        mu_andrade;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable T;  from 235 K;  to 300 K;  n 27; }
        state       { P 1 bar;  composition { NH3 1.0; } }
        thermo      { transport { liquid { viscosity { model Andrade; } } } }
        properties  ( viscosity_liquid );
        output      { file mu_andrade.csv; }
    }
);
